{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 46, :comments ["<b>Which I testify against you this day.</b> In the song of Ha'azinu I testify and warn Israel, that just as the blessed El gave them sustenance without distress in order that they serve Him, so will He destroy them when they cause them to miss His intent." "<b>Which you shall command your children.</b> At the end of your days, mention in your charge to your children all these things, and command them to guard their souls most carefully lest they corrupt them, as David commanded his son Solomon." "<b>To observe to do.</b> So that the children will observe and do."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:23:26.571964401Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}